Phase B of android-handoever.md (D1/F1, the reversal half): the AndroidConnector dies. It was never a connector — emitted no events, rejected send() (ADR-022 contract violation), and existed as a UX tile whose config row secretly drove every tool call's device resolution. Phase A (previous commit) moved that to the top-level android config; this commit removes the type entirely: core/src/connectors/android.rs, the cfg'd mod line, the registry match arm, registry::validate_connector_config (its ONLY caller was the android early-return in routes/connectors.rs test_connector — also removed; other connectors' /test intentionally stays a config-shape check), the frontend Connectors-grid tile + add-form block, and the now-dead ValidationResult/serde_json::Value imports.

DB compat: existing 'android' connector rows are ignored, not deleted — unknown-type rows already render with a fallback icon and pass /test as a shape-check no-op (comment updated in connectors.rs). Nothing reads them since Phase A; users who set serial/tcp there must re-enter under android config (known installs: fahreza's dev box only).

ADR-024 updated in the same commit: decision 4 records android as a tool-for-any-agent (pilot preset removed, guidance in tool descriptions); decision 6 rewritten as the connector REVERSAL with the why, and notes an android connector may return later as an honest event source (SMS→agent, design captured in android-handoever.md §5 — that future connector reuses the same filename with the opposite meaning, per D4 write a note when it lands).

Verified: cargo check -p cli with and without --features android, zero warnings.
